1627	  /**
1628	   * The manager brief. Everything above the floor used to be transport
1629	   * controls and a money figure; a first-time player had to infer tonight's
1630	   * target from a "/190" suffix and infer the next move from nothing at all.
1631	   * This band tracks the three conditions that can lose the night, names the
1632	   * one thing to do now, and keeps the last decision's receipt on screen
1633	   * after its toast has faded (#304).
1634	   *
1635	   * Kept quiet on purpose. Only a condition in trouble gets colour — a band
1636	   * of green chips reads as urgent when nothing is wrong, and then has no
1637	   * louder register left for when something is. Same reason the tag does not
1638	   * pulse for an open decision: the card is already modal and the top bar
1639	   * already flashes NEEDS A CALL, so a third alarm only adds noise.
1640	   *
1641	   * The content is computed by `arenaBrief`, which is pure and tested; this
1642	   * only lays it out. The training coach feeds the same "now" line rather
1643	   * than getting a banner of its own, so there is exactly one place on
1644	   * screen that answers "what do I do".
